WEBVTT

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.240
What's are you doing?

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.700
Jonathan?

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.290
Take this!

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:01.600
I did it!

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:18.830
Jonathan!

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.500
Are you all right?

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.300
Jonathan...

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.760
Remy!

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.390
Rakando!

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.640
Is that the Remy from their side?

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.190
He got swallowed up by the Energy Cube
and ended up like that.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.320
Tohru, something's coming out!

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.590
Everyone, listen up!

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.020
There's something important...

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.560
...I want to tell you!

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.200
The Dead End, the ultimate weapon?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.660
Battlefield: The Price of Bloodshed

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.370
You're saying Remy
turned into that thing?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.200
But it's true.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.330
That's what the Timekeepers
are trying to create.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.380
The Energy Cube I used to escape
changed within the sand.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.210
With this, I'm sure...

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:20.010
Tohru!

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.850
I don't know what you heard from that ghost.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:32.270
But to me, it seems more likely
you saw some illusion within that sand.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.600
Kyohma!

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.150
How can you be certain the sand
isn't a new weapon these guys created?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:41.150
Stop talking nonsense!
Our Jonathan was killed!

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.530
Says the guy that shot Kyoka!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.320
Hold on!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.120
That's right! Hold on!

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.120
That clump of sand wants a fight with us.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:56.000
And to ignore it and clobber each other
is something only morons would do.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.210
Indeed?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.970
Hey, this is only temporary.
I'll be sure to kill you later.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.300
That's my line.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.150
So that's Rakando.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.860
He's said to be the last of the "Bankara" men.
You could say he's something of a living relic.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.700
I never quite know how to deal with him.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.950
Did you send the data from the Energy Cube
over to Dr. Odhner?

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.250
Yeah, we're waiting for the results.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.630
Wonderful!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:48.640
I see. So this was the secret
to unleashing the potential of spacetime?

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:54.140
Wonderful. The experiments we've been running
until now can't even compare to this!

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.570
Thanks, Xi.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:05.110
Dr. Odhner is very excited.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:09.240
Why is his brain releasing
that quantity of chemicals?

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:13.120
Aaron said that the doctor is a brilliant man,

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.960
but he's the type that thinks nobody recognizes his genius.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.710
I believe everyone recognizes
the doctor's genius.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.170
I think so, too.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.180
But in reality, he's on
the Katagiri clan's leash,

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.350
and has to do whatever the Immature Lord Kyohma says.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.560
If I were Dr. Odhner, I'd think some frustration
would be building up.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:39.100
If I could have understood
human emotions of that sort,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.110
would I have been able
to better interact with Remy?

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.610
You're basically taking the place
of Remy's parents, aren't you?

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.030
Yes. I am a substitute.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:51.660
I-I'm sorry! That's not what I meant, Xi.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:56.790
It's fine. That's why I will do
what must be done.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:09.380
I... I don't want to...

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.850
Help me.... Help...

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:25.650
All we can carry via time travel are personal rifles and portable modules.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.990
The biggest thing we can carry
is about the size of Jonathan's powered suit.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.700
In the First Cross-Border Operation,

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:35.830
they were supposedly contemplating
bringing a suitcase nuke.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:36.910
So I've heard.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.250
But...

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:44.380
The risks from carrying unstable radioactive substances
during time travel were too great,

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.250
and that plan was abandoned.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.010
Those circumstances seem to be 
the same on the other side.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.350
Though the me on their side supposedly died...

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:58.430
That's someone else. Don't worry about it.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:04.520
Here!

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.980
Are you all right, Jonathan?

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.070
Thanks...

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.740
It looks like you're working too hard.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.790
I know that...

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.920
Because of the effects of the Dead End,
the spacetime potential has stabilized,

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.710
so the amount of time we can stay in this era has been extended.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:27.300
But, we don't know
how long that's going to last.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:33.430
Jonathan! That's not what I am talking about!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.640
You're not the one who died.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:45.020
I know... I know that...

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:50.530
I-I'm sorry.
That I wasn't able to comfort you...

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.080
<i>Can I change the future?</i>

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:03.620
<i>Can I stop everything
from turning into the Dead End?</i>

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.210
However, the birth of Dead End
is an inevitable course of history...

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.380
A few irregulars... the result... same...

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.760
Here. You have a phone call.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.350
A phone call? For me?

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.100
Yeah.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:27.610
Keep it short.
Time-phones eat up energy like crazy.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.280
Hello?

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:33.700
Tohru?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.080
I'm so glad you're alright.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.330
<i>That's my line.</i>

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.580
Yeah... I'll be fine.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.380
I'm sorry I can't help you.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:55.970
<i>It's all right.
I promise I'll rescue Remy and come back.</i>

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.060
<i>When I do, let's go to school together.</i>

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.930
<i>You think we can go to school?</i>

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:09.770
I'm sure we can.
We're fighting to bring back that everyday life.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.400
<i>You know, I...
I want to talk with you more, Tohru.</i>

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:15.900
I do, too...

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.490
<i>That's a promise.</i>

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:31.590
I wanted to protect Tohru.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:40.140
Yes, Brian Odhner speaking.
Excuse me, but who is this?

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.480
Yes... yes.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:55.150
And that's the final form
of the Desert Syndrome, a.k.a. the Dead End.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:58.410
It's expanding its spatial potential.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.200
If it continues its growth,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.830
it will start affecting the original spacetime
from this Shadow Layer.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.500
What's a Shadow Layer?

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.620
You know how the humans over here
look like shadows, right?

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.090
No matter what we do,
they don't get hurt.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:17.220
Even if the buildings look like they were destroyed,
they haven't actually been destroyed.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:19.510
A world of shadows, overlapping layers...

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.930
And so it's called the "Shadow Layer," huh?

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:27.060
But if something directly affects the time axis,
the people of this era will die.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.440
No way!

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.350
Our timeline itself might be eradicated.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:37.150
We speculate that the Dead End,
after gaining the ability to affect the time axis,

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:40.320
will affect our timelines
by surpassing the Shadow Layer.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.530
So what does this all mean?

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:47.290
We can assume both worlds will turn into sand all at once
and be swallowed up by the Dead End.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.750
Before that happens,
we're going to dismantle the Dead End.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:58.050
Remy Odhner, who absorbed an Energy Cube,
is the core of the Dead End.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.220
If we can eliminate that,

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:04.680
the Dead End should cease all functions,
just like a cell without a nucleus.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.100
Eliminate?
We're going to rescue him, right?

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.520
Whether or not Remy's alive isn't the issue.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:13.100
The issue is that he's become the core of the Dead End.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:13.860
Kyohma!

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.900
If we can rescue him, that would be ideal.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.320
In that case—

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.150
But we don't have the means.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.570
I've got it!

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:26.200
If we use the Energy Cube that's inside my guns
like when I escaped earlier,

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.830
we might be able to interfere
with the sand and destroy it.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.500
Then it's settled.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.210
You go rescue Remy.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.290
You believe me?

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.760
We'll use any means possible to survive.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.680
That's how we survived in those wastelands.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.140
I'm not going to let that homeland be destroyed,

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:50.890
even if that means working together with you.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.150
Make sure you rescue him.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:02.150
It's not pleasant for me to have someone
 with my face do a half-assed job.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:04.990
I understand.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.280
We are not the pawns of the Timekeepers.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.330
Start the operation!

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.170
You cannot do anything.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:22.380
Your intervention will only make things easier for us.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:27.220
You are, no matter what happens...

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.520
...our ally.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.230
You're the center of attention again.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:38.520
I wonder if that's
how the stars are aligning?

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:39.730
Kyohma?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.400
Take this.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.530
This is Sidune's?

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.830
Well, it's not to my taste, but...

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:55.330
It's a protective charm.
She was worried about you.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:00.920
That Timekeeper showed up
looking like Sidune, of all people.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.260
That's one thing I'll never forgive them for.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.130
Kyohma!

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.890
That's right. I think so, too.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:24.400
Help... Help me...

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:25.990
Everyone....

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:29.530
Everyone is...

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.750
Stop! Stop it!

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.840
Help me! Help me, Xi!

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:43.960
Xi!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.520
Xi! Xi!

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.650
I'm right here.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.820
It's not just me.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.070
Kyoka's here too.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.700
So everything's all right.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.290
It's fine.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.420
There's nothing to fear, Remy.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.270
<i>That enemy.... It looks a lot like Xi.</i>

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:46.400
Jonathan!

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.820
Leave this to me!
The PUG's armor can handle it!

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:57.160
Hurry! I won't screw up like my other self did!

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:57.950
Got it!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.050
Don't die until I kill you!

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:16.930
The same goes for you.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:23.230
It is almost time for your role in this to end.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.870
Dammit, this is endless.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.290
Thanks, Kusakage...

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:45.750
Sir Aaron...

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:51.170
Have I been able
to fight valiantly, as a man?

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:54.220
Yeah, so stop talking.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:17:03.400
I'm glad... I... I wanted to prove
that I was a man.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.230
That was all.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.400
Kusakage! Rakando, too!

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.860
Lyudmila made an emergency escape?

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.280
At this rate, they're all done for!

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:55.820
Xi?

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:24.390
Xi! That's crazy!

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:27.850
Stop...

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:34.360
Stop... Xi... Xi is going to protect me...

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.240
Remy! I'll save you now!

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:52.090
Releasing spacetime phase transition reactor final safety mechanism!

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:09.650
Goodbye, Remy. May you find happiness...

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.820
I will protect you.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.120
Xi!

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.290
Damn it!

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.850
What's going on? Status report!

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.770
<i>It's some kind of unknown spacetime storm!</i>

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:31.480
<i>I can't observe
the synchronized time axis of 2015!</i>

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.900
Remy! Snap out of it!

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.610
Remy! Remy!

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:51.000
I had no idea you were capable of dismantling a Dead End that had developed to this point.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:57.050
I'm forced to declare this interference experiment a failure, I suppose.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:00.130
Then, stop doing senseless things
like this from now on.

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:05.180
Our interventions already
reach everywhere in the world.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:11.940
The two worlds learned the value of Energy Cubes
and made travel between each other possible.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:18.070
I'm sure that you will create another Dead End
of your own accord very soon.

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.780
I won't let that happen!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:25.160
You have opened Pandora's Box
with your own hands.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:28.740
<b><i>SUDDEN TURN </i></b>THE PRICE OF ARROGANCE

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.830
Next episode: "Sudden Turn."

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:28.410
"The Price of Arrogance."

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:30.200
Wait, it's over so suddenly?

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:33.030
Breaking the template!
Breaking apart stagnant episode previews!

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.950
The well-love standards are important too.

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:38.370
A surprise has to betray the expectations
and predictions of everyone!
